  "failedDom": " Welcome Visitors\n\nWelcome to this Federated Wiki site. From this page you can find who we are and what we do. New sites provide this information and then claim the site as their own. You will need your own site to participate.\n\nPages about us.\n\n Ralf Barkow — See How I Use My Wiki\n\nPages where we do and share.\n\n⚠ WARNING: Chrome is introducing/rolling out Local Network Access permission behavior for pages that attempt connections to local network targets. blog , docs , draft \n\nThe following reference is to a local network target.\n\n Getting Started with HyperDoc on macOS (Nix, direnv, SBCL) — HyperDoc is a Common Lisp system for serving hypertext documents with interactive CLOG-based inspectors.\n\n Running a private Wiki on your computer — explains that if private pages with localhost in fork history get published, other users’ browsers may attempt local connections and show security warnings; suggested fix is to use a host alias like: 127.0.0.1 wiki.local\n\n HyperDoc Tutorial — HyperDoc Navigation Basics\n\n Focused Semantic Source Stations — Focused semantic source stations is a reusable view type for rendering semantically meaningful stations inside source so users can lay durable routes from source to annotations or related objects without editing files inline.\n\nYou can edit your copy of these pages. Press [+] to add more writing spaces. Read How to Wiki for more ideas. Follow Recent Changes here and nearby.\n\nCC BY-SA 4.0 . JSON . hyperdoc.dreyeck.ch . search\n\n Trails Rendered\n\nHere we work out an example to use as a test case. This page saved from Pattern Machinery.\n\nHoward\nBecker\nEveryday\nDonald\nSchön\nJohn\nDewey\nSusan\nLeigh\nStar\nReflective\nPractice\nInteraction\nDesign\nHenrik\nGedenryd\nSusan\nKare\nAlan\nCooper\nInteresting\nPeople\nAndrew\nAbbott\nClose\nAt\nHand\nDorothy\nSmith\nEthnomethodology\nJean\nLave\nlakoff\nund\njohnson\n\nINCLUDED\n  3 aspects\n\nview in solo\n\nWe will add two trails by hand then explore how they interact while browsing aspects.\n\nSusan Kare ⇒ John Dewey ⇒ Reflective Practice\n\nJean Lave ⇒ Dorothy Smith ⇒ Reflective Practice\n\nCLICK CODE trails CLICK SOLO CLICK PREVIEW synopsis items help\n\nimport {Graph} from 'https://wardcunningham.github.io/graph/graph.js'\nexport function trails () {\n let context = this.context\n let page = context.page\n let result = page.story\n  .filter(item => item.type == \"paragraph\")\n  .map(item => item.text)\n  .filter(text => text.startsWith('[['))\n  .map((text,i) => ({\n   name:`trail ${i+1}`,   \n   graph: trail(text.split(/ . /))\n  }))\n this.aspect = [{\n  id:context.itemId,\n  source:page.title,\n  result}]\n this.items = [{\n  type: \"solo\",\n  text: \"LINEUP\\nINCLUDED\",\n  aspects: result\n },'See [[Solo Lineup Browser]]']\n return `${result.length} aspects`\n}\n\nSee Increment of Progress, Eigenmode Patterns\n\nfunction trail(names) {\n let graph = new Graph()\n let prev = null\n for (let each of names) {\n  let name = each\n   .replaceAll(/[\\[\\]]/g,\"\")\n   .replaceAll(/ +/g,\"\\n\")\n  let nid = graph.addNode(\"\",{name})\n  if(prev !== null) graph.addRel(\"Trail\",prev,nid,{})\n  prev = nid\n }\n return graph\n}\n1 pages link here:\nCC BY-SA 4.0 . JSON . hyperdoc.dreyeck.ch . search\nSite Owned by: Ralf Barkow       430 pages \n  ☰   wiki  ",
